## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; narrowed to this round's scope; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta (C1, C2).** A path beyond the three, a changed `server.js` line other than the one approved line, a changed list entry or answer text, a removed old cell, a changed line in the old 38 cells = **Blocker**; a person's name, customer name, secret or decision-card id in an added line or the message = **Blocker**; non-ASCII, `.only/.skip/.todo`, a retry, a suppression comment, a loosened existing assertion = **Major**; a brief or work-number token in an added line = **Minor**; a head other than `eccfa60e` = STOP.
- **G-2 exposure and behaviour (C5, C6, C7).** A head acceptance neither base-valid nor an admissible strict hit, a different user than base where a base-valid candidate exists, a pronoun-lead bypass, `rosterLogs` or rows in a response, log line, prompt or context = **Blocker**; the two-distinct-hits rule showing a user = **Blocker**, differing from base on a pair = **Major**; a C6 figure differing from B912's for an array or null read = **Major** (a regression the guard line should not cause); an answer text differing from base for a message the ruling says is unchanged = **Major**; a roster read on a message with no candidate = **Major**; a failure path that crashes, leaks rows or connection text, or answers HTTP 500 / an error body at head where base answers a normal answer = **Major**; where base and head both answer an error class, or the head is the better class = **Note** (the base difference of the addendum belongs here when every shape it covers meets the class rule).
